      "conclusions": [
        "Exact guest capability is required for create/context/cancel, including with owner cookie. Creation requires writable status; closed valid capability can read/withdraw. Current guest SQL predicates and egress assertions deny expired/revoked/foreign access. Owner page uses current owner guard plus existing VPS per-statement/session and response authorization.",
        "Origin plus versioned explicit consent, request, audit and existing outbox share one atomic batch. Deferred request FK prevents orphan origins. Unique conversation/key plus existing dedupe and payload hash preserve idempotency under races without email joining identities.",
        "Receipts/pages expose only local id, status, version, createdAt, safe ERP status; cursor is bounded canonical timestamp/UUID, no token or PII. Page size20 and exact own-conversation join apply on every page.",
        "Current stored conversation locale and configured service mapping drive the existing ERP envelope. Assistant source attribution is empty. Free-text message/chat/token/conversation ID are excluded; no new ERP wire or credential persistence.",
        "Withdrawal uses version/state CAS and current guest fence, including after chat closure. Existing dispatcher blocks unattempted cancelled sources, preserves APPLIED and records UNKNOWN for cancellation racing already-started delivery. Withdrawal is not remote erasure.",
        "Disabled bridge initially creates real PENDING/null-pinned queue; maintenance changes it to BLOCKED/MAPPING_NOT_PINNED with zero transport. Browser render fixture explicitly pauses maintenance to inspect initial PENDING; it makes no scheduler acceptance claim.",
        "Migration0017 adds exactly one table to22 unchanged snapshot definitions, preserves all prior journal entries, has deferred request FK and immutable origin trigger. Actual restore validates legacy and new graphs; old binary fails closed on newer ledger.",
        "Portal-history fixture now compares exact ordered canonical filenames in live and restored DB; obsolete count16 was incorrect. All existing message/history/integrity assertions remain."
      ],
